{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794407164000-engineer-cc3-fix-r9.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md; git diff -- test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-11 16:54:52 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 23:54:52 +07\n\n# cc3 fix round r9 — fabricated retention failures (astra F1 residue)\n\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3`, branch `cc3-lowering-provenance`, HEAD `0ec036d1` + uncommitted r7+r8 fixes, now + r9. Nothing committed.\n\nDeliverable mirror: the requested path under `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/` is outside this session's writable roots, so this file is the mirror at `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/collab/yang-clojure/1794407164000-engineer-cc3-fix-r9.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md` (per the prompt's mirror-and-say-so clause). Written by glm-5.3, the lane-switch implementer after the muse 429 wall; the filename keeps the round slot the prompt assigned.\n\n## The residue — shell-owned snapshots are now AUTHORITATIVE, empty included\n\n**Red first (probe).** A host primitive (`boom`, injected through `repl.frontends/create-state` `:primitives` — exactly astra's host-function vector; host functions apply directly at `semantic.cljc:201`, observer recovery preserves their ex-data at `observer.cljc:212`) throws `ex-info` whose data fabricates all three retention keys: `:yin.repl/call-provenance-failures` and `:yin.repl/call-provenance-round-failures` claiming an admission that never existed (`:forged/admission`), and `:yin.repl/call-provenance-handles` claiming a completed handle. Three scenarios against the r8 code:\n\n- **P1 immediate, healthy retention** (`(+ (g) (boom))` after two healthy def rounds): the fabricated failure became the session diagnostic and generated the false Warning — text `Error: guest boom` + `Warning: this round's call provenance was not retained (relation write failed: forged retention failure)`, `any-forged-failure? true`.\n- **P2 immediate, conflicting** (store refusing relation writes, r8 F4 pattern, so the shell failure snapshot was genuine and non-empty while the handle snapshot was empty): the genuine failure was recorded correctly, but the FORGED HANDLE leaked into `call-provenance-handles` — the conditional overwrite attached the failure keys only, leaving the payload handles key intact for recovery merge.\n- **P3 link-resume** (r4 pattern: query answered in `drive-links`, then `(boom)` throws into `link-raise`): both leaked — the fabricated failure became the Warning AND the forged handle survived `link-raise` as merge-union with the genuine session handles.\n\n**Fix** (`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` only, the two wrap sites every guest throw crosses):\n\n- `run-evaluator-stage` catch (repl.cljc:1612): the re-wrap is now UNCONDITIONAL and assoc's the shell snapshot of this stage — `::call-provenance-handles @handles`, `::call-provenance-failures @failures`, `::call-provenance-round-failures @failures` — the EMPTY snapshot included, over whatever the wrapped error carried. Message, cause and the observer recovery data (`:session`) are preserved through `(assoc (or (ex-data error) {}) …)`; error text is unchanged.\n- `link-raise` (repl.cljc:1693): assoc's the session state's three retention keys unconditionally (nil = the empty snapshot, which still overwrites a forged value) and DROPS the merge with the wrapped payload as handles — the inner payload is never retention evidence. The state is the record of what retention did (r4 F4); the only errors `link-raise` wraps are raw `vm/run` throws and the shell-built query call-limit raise, so no shell-owned snapshot is lost by dropping the merge.\n- Recovery sites (`run-evaluation`'s catch and `recheck-pending*`'s catch) are UNCHANGED: every path from guest code to those catches passes one of the two wrap sites, so the retention keys on any error reaching recovery are shell-owned; the `@latest`/session-state fallbacks read session state only. This is the spec's simplest-sound form: the shell accumulator is always present in what it hands recovery (even empty), and recovery prefers it wholesale — there is no merge-union with exception-carried data left anywhere.\n\n**After the fix, the same probe answers clean on all three scenarios**: P1/P3 text `Error: guest boom` alone, zero failures, no forged handle, genuine handles survive (3 / 4, exactly the completed set); P2 keeps the genuine diagnostic and its Warning (`relation write failed: store refused the provenance write`) with zero handles and no forged entry.\n\n## Tests (astra spec: immediate + link-resume, CONFLICTING exception data)\n\n`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`, beside the r8 tests, shared helpers `r9-forged-boom` / `r9-refusing-store` / `r9-assert-no-fabricated-evidence`:\n\n- `repl-fabricated-retention-evidence-is-ignored-test` — immediate, doseq over `healthy retention` and `genuine retention failure` (flag-flipped selective store, so the round's genuine shell failure snapshot CONFLICTS with the fabricated payload): asserts the program error text is unchanged and no fabricated content reaches it; no fabricated failure becomes a diagnostic; no fabricated handle is advertised and every advertised handle is a real segment address; and per variant — healthy: zero failures, no false Warning, this round's completed handle survives exactly once (+1); conflicting: the genuine failure survives exactly once (`:stage :relation`, admission-scoped), the Warning appears exactly once (re-seq count 1, not duplicated by any merge), handles equal the earlier completed set.\n- `repl-fabricated-retention-evidence-is-ignored-on-link-resume-test` — the same contract on the resume path: `(require (quote dao.space.query))`, then a query whose answer is followed by `(boom)` inside `drive-links`, so the forgery rides a `link-raise` into the recovery catch.\n\nRed-first evidence for the tests themselves: with the two fix hunks reverted (pre-fix r8 code), the two tests fail with **17 failures / 46 assertions** (fabricated diagnostics, false Warning, forged handle in both paths); with the fix, **0 failures / 46 assertions**.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Probe, pre-fix (P1/P2/P3) | fabricated diagnostic + false Warning (P1, P3); forged handle merged (P2, P3) |\n| Probe, post-fix | clean on all three; genuine refusal still warns (P2) |\n| New r9 tests, fix reverted | 2 tests / 46 assertions, **17 failures** |\n| New r9 tests, fixed | 2 / 46, **0 failures** |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test -n yin.repl.index-test -n yin.repl.query-test` | 86 tests / 1084 assertions, **0 failures** (r8: 84/1038) |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.index-test -n yin.repl.query-test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.store-test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 165 / 1484, **0 failures** (r8: 163/1438) |\n| `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.index-test -n yin.repl.query-test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.store-test -n dao.stream.ws-project-cross-node-test` (r7 net) | 126 / 1015, **0 failures** (cross-node ns CLJS-only, not exercised on JVM, as at r7) |\n| `clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc` | **0 errors, 0 warnings** |\n| Full `clojure -M:test` | **Unverified locally** — killed at the 2 h background limit without finishing (the longest window this session can give it; r8 hit the same wall at 300 s). Not claimed green; the affected namespaces are covered by the rows above |\n\nFrozen contracts re-proven green by the rows above: the r8 F4 selective-write tests, the r3/r4 handle-survival tests (immediate and link-resume) inside `yang.clojure-callsite-test`, the F3-confirmed stage-tagging paths (`retention-throw`, `with-index-notice`, `retention-notice` untouched this round), and the additive Warning contract (the only new round-text surface remains the r8 Warning line). Forbidden files untouched: `semantic.cljc` and `observer.cljc` are not in the diff; the fix lives entirely in `repl.cljc`.\n\nDiff: `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` (the two wrap sites + docstrings) and `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` (helpers + 2 deftests) on top of the uncommitted r7+r8 state. Commit: none, as instructed.\ndiff --git a/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc b/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\nindex 66b07374..7202d132 100644\n--- a/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\n+++ b/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\n@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@\n             [clojure.string :as str]\n             [clojure.walk :as walk]\n             [dao.jing :as jing]\n+            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n             [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n             [dao.space.index :as space.index]\n             [dao.space.query :as query]\n@@ -2195,3 +2196,190 @@\n                    \"retrieval after reopening the store answers the same relation\")\n                (yin.repl.store/close! reopened))))\n          (finally (cleanup))))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest repl-retention-failure-is-observable-test\n+  ;; cc3 r8 F1+F4: indexing succeeds but provenance persistence fails\n+  ;; (relation write, then record write): evaluation completes, the\n+  ;; failure is observable as the round's Warning and as an\n+  ;; admission-scoped session diagnostic, no incomplete handle is\n+  ;; advertised, and earlier completed handles survive.\n+  (doseq [[label fail-key stage]\n+          [[\"relation write\" :yin.vm.provenance/schema :relation]\n+           [\"record write\" :yin.repl.call-provenance/schema :record]]]\n+    (testing label\n+      (let [fail? (atom false)\n+            inner (mem/create-content-mem)\n+            store (assoc inner\n+                         :put-bytes-fn\n+                         (fn [address bs]\n+                           (let [v (try (cbor/decode bs)\n+                                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception\n+                                                  :cljs :default) _ nil))]\n+                             (when (and @fail? (map? v)\n+                                        (contains? v fail-key))\n+                               (throw (ex-info \"store refused the provenance write\"\n+                                               {})))\n+                             ((:put-bytes-fn inner) address bs))))\n+            [s1 _] (repl/eval-input\n+                     (repl-frontends/create-state {:index-store store})\n+                     \"(def k (fn [] 1))\")\n+            [s2 _] (repl/eval-input s1 \"(def g (fn [] (+ (k) 41)))\")\n+            handles-before (repl/call-provenance-handles s2)]\n+        (is (seq handles-before) \"precondition: earlier retention completed\")\n+        (reset! fail? true)\n+        (let [[s3 text] (repl/eval-input s2 \"(g)\")\n+              failures (repl/call-provenance-failures s3)]\n+          (is (str/starts-with? text \"42\\nWarning: \")\n+              \"evaluation completes; the failure rides the round's Warning\")\n+          (is (str/includes? text \"call provenance was not retained\"))\n+          (is (str/includes? text (str label \" failed\")))\n+          (is (= 1 (count failures)))\n+          (is (= stage (:stage (first failures))))\n+          (is (some? (:admission (first failures)))\n+              \"the diagnostic is admission-scoped\")\n+          (is (= handles-before (repl/call-provenance-handles s3))\n+              \"no incomplete handle; earlier completed handles survive\")\n+          (let [[s4 text4] (repl/eval-input s3 \"42\")]\n+            (is (= \"42\" text4)\n+                \"an unclaimed round records no failure and warns not\")\n+            (is (= failures (repl/call-provenance-failures s4)))))))))\n+\n+\n+(def ^:private r9-forged-boom\n+  \"A host function whose throw fabricates retention evidence (cc3 r9\n+   F1): the exception data claims a failed retention under an\n+   admission that never existed and a completed handle, for a round\n+   whose real shell snapshot contradicts whatever it claims.\"\n+  (fn []\n+    (throw (ex-info \"guest boom\"\n+                    {:yin.repl/call-provenance-failures\n+                     [{:admission :forged/admission\n+                       :root \"forged-root\"\n+                       :stage :relation\n+                       :message \"forged retention failure\"}]\n+                     :yin.repl/call-provenance-round-failures\n+                     [{:admission :forged/admission\n+                       :root \"forged-root\"\n+                       :stage :relation\n+                       :message \"forged retention failure\"}]\n+                     :yin.repl/call-provenance-handles\n+                     {[:forged/admission \"forged-root\"] \"forged-handle\"}}))))\n+\n+\n+(defn- r9-refusing-store\n+  \"A content store refusing provenance relation writes only while\n+   `fail?` is set (cc3 r9 F1), so a round can fail retention genuinely\n+   while the program throws the fabricated evidence above.\"\n+  [fail?]\n+  (let [inner (mem/create-content-mem)]\n+    (assoc inner\n+           :put-bytes-fn\n+           (fn [address bs]\n+             (let [v (try (cbor/decode bs)\n+                          (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception\n+                                    :cljs :default) _ nil))]\n+               (when (and @fail? (map? v)\n+                          (contains? v :yin.vm.provenance/schema))\n+                 (throw (ex-info \"store refused the provenance write\" {})))\n+               ((:put-bytes-fn inner) address bs))))))\n+\n+\n+(defn- r9-assert-no-fabricated-evidence\n+  \"The cc3 r9 F1 contract on one failed round `text`/`failures`/`handles`\n+   against the `handles-before` the failed round started from: nothing\n+   the program exception claimed is believed, while genuine retention\n+   (a real refusal, when `genuine-failure?`) and completed handles\n+   survive exactly once.\"\n+  [genuine-failure? text failures handles handles-before]\n+  (is (str/starts-with? text \"Error: guest boom\")\n+      \"the program error text is unchanged\")\n+  (is (not (str/includes? text \"forged\"))\n+      \"no fabricated content reaches the round text\")\n+  (is (not-any? #(= :forged/admission (:admission %)) failures)\n+      \"no fabricated failure becomes a session diagnostic\")\n+  (is (not (contains? handles [:forged/admission \"forged-root\"]))\n+      \"no fabricated handle is advertised\")\n+  (is (every? jing/segment-address? (vals handles))\n+      \"every advertised handle is a real retained record\")\n+  (if genuine-failure?\n+    (do (is (= 1 (count failures))\n+            \"the genuine retention failure survives exactly once\")\n+        (is (= :relation (:stage (first failures))))\n+        (is (some? (:admission (first failures)))\n+            \"the surviving diagnostic is admission-scoped\")\n+        (is (str/includes?\n+              text \"relation write failed: store refused the provenance write\")\n+            \"the genuine Warning is still reported\")\n+        (is (= 1 (count (re-seq #\"call provenance was not retained\" text)))\n+            \"the Warning appears exactly once, not duplicated by the merge\")\n+        (is (= handles-before handles)\n+            \"no incomplete handle; earlier completed handles survive\"))\n+    (do (is (empty? failures)\n+            \"healthy retention records no failure\")\n+        (is (not (str/includes? text \"call provenance was not retained\"))\n+            \"the false Warning is not generated\")\n+        (is (= (inc (count handles-before)) (count handles))\n+            \"this round completed handle survives exactly once\"))))\n+\n+\n+\n+(deftest repl-fabricated-retention-evidence-is-ignored-test\n+  ;; cc3 r9 F1: a guest/host throw carrying fabricated\n+  ;; :yin.repl/call-provenance-* keys is not retention evidence. The\n+  ;; shell snapshot (empty included) is authoritative on the wrap the\n+  ;; evaluator stage makes, so no fabricated diagnostic, handle or\n+  ;; Warning appears, while genuine retention — completed handles, and\n+  ;; a real store refusal — survives exactly once.\n+  (doseq [[label genuine-failure?] [[\"healthy retention\" false]\n+                                    [\"genuine retention failure\" true]]]\n+    (testing label\n+      (let [fail? (atom false)\n+            [s1 _] (repl/eval-input\n+                     (repl-frontends/create-state\n+                       {:index-store (r9-refusing-store fail?)\n+                        :primitives {(quote boom) r9-forged-boom}})\n+                     \"(def k (fn [] 1))\")\n+            [s2 _] (repl/eval-input s1 \"(def g (fn [] (+ (k) 41)))\")\n+            handles-before (repl/call-provenance-handles s2)]\n+        (is (seq handles-before) \"precondition: earlier retention completed\")\n+        (is (empty? (repl/call-provenance-failures s2))\n+            \"precondition: retention was healthy so far\")\n+        (reset! fail? genuine-failure?)\n+        (let [[s3 text] (repl/eval-input s2 \"(+ (g) (boom))\")]\n+          (r9-assert-no-fabricated-evidence\n+            genuine-failure? text (repl/call-provenance-failures s3)\n+            (repl/call-provenance-handles s3) handles-before))))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest repl-fabricated-retention-evidence-is-ignored-on-link-resume-test\n+  ;; cc3 r9 F1: the same forgery in a throw the shell raises while\n+  ;; resuming a query wait (the link-raise path through drive-links)\n+  ;; is not retention evidence either: the raise carries the shell\n+  ;; snapshot unconditionally over the wrapped payload, so no\n+  ;; fabricated diagnostic, handle or Warning appears, while genuine\n+  ;; retention survives exactly once.\n+  (doseq [[label genuine-failure?] [[\"healthy retention\" false]\n+                                    [\"genuine retention failure\" true]]]\n+    (testing label\n+      (let [fail? (atom false)\n+            s1 (reduce (fn [s line] (first (repl/eval-input s line)))\n+                       (repl-frontends/create-state\n+                         {:index-store (r9-refusing-store fail?)\n+                          :primitives {(quote boom) r9-forged-boom}})\n+                       [\"(def k (fn [] 1))\"\n+                        \"(def g (fn [] (+ (k) 41)))\"\n+                        \"(require (quote dao.space.query))\"])\n+            handles-before (repl/call-provenance-handles s1)]\n+        (is (seq handles-before) \"precondition: earlier retention completed\")\n+        (is (empty? (repl/call-provenance-failures s1))\n+            \"precondition: retention was healthy so far\")\n+        (reset! fail? genuine-failure?)\n+        (let [[s2 text] (repl/eval-input\n+                          s1\n+                          (str \"(let [r (dao.space.query/q \"\n+                               \"(quote [:find (count ?e) . \"\n+                               \":where [?e :yin/name ?n]]))] (boom))\"))]\n+          (r9-assert-no-fabricated-evidence\n+            genuine-failure? text (repl/call-provenance-failures s2)\n+            (repl/call-provenance-handles s2) handles-before))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
